  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Young African Leaders Initiative (YALI) - Connected Women</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mobile penetration in Kenya is above 90 percent. Despite the high penetration, access to smartphones by women remains low in rural areas mainly due to the high cost. Smartphones and mobile-based financial literacy can transform the lives of women at the base of the economic pyramid. We provide smartphones to customers who repay them in daily installments of $0.18 via mobile money for a period of 10 months. The phones have transformed how the tailors source their fabric, access new trends and how they communicate with clients.</narrative>
  </description>
